{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01JP8sfacWqQAau684L4ToJ7", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brabham_BT46\"}, {\"url\": \"https://motorsportmagazine.com/archive/article/february-2025/88/1978-brabham-bt46b-fan-car\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.wikipedia.org/wiki/BT46\"}, {\"url\": \"https://roarington.com/media-house/directories/cars/brabham_bt46b_1978\"}, {\"url\": \"https://automobile.fandom.com/wiki/1978_Swedish_Grand_Prix\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.supercars.net/blog/brabham-bt46b-fan-car\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/special-article/the-75-greatest-grands-prix/6/75-1978-swedish-gp-brabham-fan-car-wins-its-one-and-only-race/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thelegocarblog.com/tag/fan-car/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.tomhartleyjnr.com/?p=128237\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thelegocarblog.com/2017/06/12/formula-1-sucks/\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T13:14:28.837Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Brabham BT46B fan car 1978 Swedish Grand Prix winner", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_015MuD23AjviiK6CY9yzxLgV", "content": [{"title": "Brabham BT46", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brabham_BT46"}, {"title": "1978 Brabham BT46B ‘fan car’", "url": "https://motorsportmagazine.com/archive/article/february-2025/88/1978-brabham-bt46b-fan-car"}, {"title": "Brabham BT46", "url": "https://www.wikipedia.org/wiki/BT46"}, {"title": "1978 Brabham BT46B", "url": "https://roarington.com/media-house/directories/cars/brabham_bt46b_1978"}, {"title": "1978 Swedish Grand Prix", "url": "https://automobile.fandom.com/wiki/1978_Swedish_Grand_Prix"}, {"title": "brabham bt46b fan car", "url": "https://www.supercars.net/blog/brabham-bt46b-fan-car"}, {"title": "75. 1978 Swedish GP: Brabham fan car wins its one and only race", "url": "https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/special-article/the-75-greatest-grands-prix/6/75-1978-swedish-gp-brabham-fan-car-wins-its-one-and-only-race/"}, {"title": "Tag Archives: Fan Car", "url": "https://thelegocarblog.com/tag/fan-car/"}, {"title": "< Previously sold", "url": "https://www.tomhartleyjnr.com/?p=128237"}, {"title": "Formula 1 Sucks", "url": "https://thelegocarblog.com/2017/06/12/formula-1-sucks/"}]}, "Niki Lauda won the 1978 Swedish Grand Prix at Anderstorp in the Brabham BT46B \"fan car,\" and it was the only race the car ran in that configuration. Sources differ on why it stopped racing. Wikipedia says the FIA had ruled the car legal for the rest of the season, yet Brabham withdrew it anyway. A Roarington page says the FIA banned it, while Motorsport Magazine reports that the result stood and Brabham pulled the car voluntarily, possibly because team owner Bernie Ecclestone had just taken over as FOCA chief and needed rivals' support.\n\nOther details: the fan was officially justified as engine cooling, but it also pulled air from under the car to create downforce. Lauda's margin was over half a minute, and the car later finished second at the British Grand Prix without the fan."], "durationSeconds": 5.998354375, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01JP8sfacWqQAau684L4ToJ7", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
